course: dictionary
lesson: 13664
title: Formal and informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Informally means in a relaxed, friendly, everyday way, without strict rules or formal manners. It is the opposite of formally. Notice the clue inside the word: informal, then -ly, which makes it an adverb about how something is done.
explain: Writers choose their words for who they will read them. «Hi Sam, see you at the park later!» is a message to a friend, so it is written informally. «Dear Councillor Jones, I am writing about the park.» goes to the council, so it is written formally.
explain: Informally can also mean unofficially, as part of no official process. «We agreed the plan informally over lunch, with no meeting and no vote.» Nothing was written down or made official. Look at the clues around the word: friends, lunch, no meeting, no vote.
fact: Informally means in a relaxed, friendly, everyday way.
fact: «Informally» can also mean unofficially, not as part of an official process.
fact: Informal writing is chatty and casual, and it may use slang. Formal writing follows stricter rules.
fact: «Dress informally» means wear casual clothes, not formal ones.
fact: «Known informally as» introduces a nickname, as in «known informally as Max».
exercise: «We agreed informally that we would meet after school.» Informally here means | Very quietly | Angrily | Officially, with a signed form | *Unofficially, without a formal process
exercise: Which would you write informally? | A letter to the head teacher asking for a day off | An official school form | A report for the council about road safety | *A chatty message to your best friend
exercise: «Sam is known informally as Sammy at home.» What does informally suggest? | *A friendly nickname used in everyday life | A formal title on a certificate | A strict rule written in a book | A secret code
test: «Please dress informally for the trip: jeans and trainers are fine.» What does dress informally mean? | Wear nothing at all | *Wear casual clothes | Wear a costume | Wear a strict uniform
test: Which sentence uses informal language? | *Hey, wanna come to the park later? | The committee shall convene on Monday. | I hereby declare the results final. | Dear Sir, I request your attendance at the meeting.
exam: Ella writes to her gran in a chatty way with slang, but she writes to the council in a serious, polite way. Which word best describes her message to her gran? | Officially | *Informally | Formally | Strictly
